{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Swarming thing of the waters.</b> They are the small creatures that were created from the waters, and in waters a living soul, male and female. And after he said, they are a detestable thing to you, he said, and they shall be a detestable thing to you, to explain what is a detestable thing, and it is: from their flesh you shall not eat. And behold, fish is called flesh — only what the sages said in [tractate] Nedarim is according to the linguistic usage of these generations. And he added, whatever has no fin and scales, to make a general rule for all waters, for at the beginning he mentioned only seas and streams."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {0 "Reading הימים (seas) for what appears to be המים (the waters) in the second occurrence; the logic requires 'seas and streams' as the initial category being generalized."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:25.719007060Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}